@page "/help"
@inherits DeckPage
<PageTitle>Help · Release Deck</PageTitle><div class="reading"><h1>Prepare and deliver a release.</h1><ol class="help-steps"><li><h2>Add your videos</h2><p>Open a release, choose Add videos and play the preview. Identify each file to confirm which original belongs to the episode.</p></li><li><h2>Prepare each episode</h2><p>Write the title, description and translations. Answer the audience and altered-content questions. Planned times use your device's local time.</p></li><li><h2>Keep a copy</h2><p>Save project file keeps an editable plan. Download release package adds a readable release sheet. Neither contains your videos; reattach the originals on another device.</p></li><li><h2>Review together</h2><p>Save online, invite a viewer or editor, and leave feedback on that saved version. Only the owner can approve it. Saving changes requires a fresh approval.</p></li><li><h2>Deliver deliberately</h2><p>The owner connects a channel and starts a private upload. If a transfer stops, Check remote status before Resume transfer. Apply approved details and choose visibility separately. A release is applied one video at a time.</p></li></ol><details><summary>Privacy and recovery</summary><p>Your browser saves local release text and file identities. Videos stay on your device until you explicitly upload to Google. Invited teammates can read shared release text and file names; channel connections and transfer access remain with the owner.</p><p>Keep your project downloads if browser storage may be cleared. Disconnecting a channel or canceling transfer access does not delete a video already on YouTube.</p></details><details><summary>Connection unavailable</summary><p>You can preview videos and download a release without connecting to YouTube.</p></details><details><summary>Troubleshooting</summary><label class="check-line"><input type="checkbox" @bind="Store.DiagnosticLogging">Log action timing and errors in this browser.</label><p>Release text, videos and channel access are excluded.</p></details></div>
